description
	original_author = <
		["date"] = <"2020-04-27">
		["name"] = <"Weronika Gujo; Katrin Tröltzsch">
		["organisation"] = <"Heidelberg Medical University">
		["email"] = <"Weronika.Gujo@med.uni-heidelberg.de">
	>
	lifecycle_state = <"published">
	details = <
		["de"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::de]>
			purpose = <"Zur Darstellung des Status der Tumorerkrankung im Verlauf oder nach dem Ende der Therapie bzw. der Nachsorge.">
			keywords = <"Residualstatus","Primärtumor","Therapie","Tumorstatus","Residualtumor","Lokalrezidiv","Tumor","Progress","Keine Veränderung","Vollremission","Teilremission","CR","PR","divergent","MR","CRr","NC","Tumorrest","Veränderung","partial remission","no change","complete remission","minimal response","residual","Tumorverlauf","Lymphknotenmetastasen","Fernmetastasen","Ausbreitung","Residuen">
			copyright = <"© HiGHmed">
			use = <"Dieser Archetyp soll verwendet werden, um die Beurteilungen zum Status des Tumors lokal, gesamt und in den Bereichen der Fernmetastasen und der regionären Lymphknoten im Verlauf oder nach dem Ende der Therapie bzw. der Nachsorge darzustellen.

Der Tumorstatus ist wichtig um den Erfolg der Therapie zu beurteilen und beschreibt die Veränderungen des Tumors nach der (Primär-) Therapie. Es soll festgestellt werden, ob zum Beispiel Tumorgewebe noch vorhanden ist; ein Progress bei vorhandenen Tumorresten (Residualtumor) vorliegt; keine Veränderungen bei vorhandenen Tumorresten (Residualtumor) oder ein Lokalrezidiv vorliegt. 
Darüber hinaus wird mit diesem Archetyp der Verlaufsstatus in Bereichen der Fernmetastasen und der regionären Lymphknoten dargestellt. 

Dieser Archetyp kann in dem Slot \"Spezifische Details\" des übergeordneten Archetyps \"Problem/Diagnose\" (openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis) eingebettet werden.">
			misuse = <"Darf nicht zur Darstellung eines Erkrankungsstatus außerhalb der Tumorerkrankung genutzt werden.">
		>
		["nb"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::nb]>
			purpose = <"Å representere statusen til en kreftsykdom i løpet av behandlingsforløpet eller etter behandling og oppfølging.">
			keywords = <"Residualstatus","primærtumor","behandling","tumorstatus","resttumor","lokalt residiv","tumor","progresjon","ingen endring","full remisjon","delvis remisjon","CR","PR","divergent","MR","CRr","NC","tumorrester","endring","partial remisjon","no change","complete remisjon","minimal response","residual","tumorforløp","lymfeknutemetastaser","fjernmetastaser","spredning","rester">
			copyright = <"© HiGHmed">
			use = <"Å representere statusen til en kreftsykdom i løpet av behandlingsforløpet eller etter behandling og oppfølging.
Bruk
Denne arketypen skal brukes for å presentere vurderinger av statusen til en tumor lokalt, totalt sett, og i områdene med fjernmetastaser og regionale lymfeknuter i løpet av behandlingsforløpet eller etter behandling og oppfølging.

Tumorstatusen er viktig for å vurdere behandlingens suksess og beskriver endringene i tumoren etter primærbehandlingen. Det skal fastslås om for eksempel tumorvev fortsatt er til stede; om det foreligger progresjon med tilstedeværende tumorrester (resttumor); ingen endringer med tilstedeværende tumorrester (resttumor) eller et lokalt residiv.
I tillegg viser denne arketypen forløpsstatusen i områdene med fjernmetastaser og regionale lymfeknuter.

Denne arketypen kan innlemmes i sporingsdetaljene til overordnet arketypen \"Problem/Diagnose\" (openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis).">
			misuse = <"Må ikke brukes til å representere sykdomsstatus utenfor kreftsykdom.">
		>
		["en"] = <
			language = <[ISO_639-1::en]>
			purpose = <"To represent the status of a tumour disease during the course of treatment or after treatment and follow-up.">
			keywords = <"residual status","primary tumour","therapy","tumour status","residual tumour","local recurrence","tumour","progression","no change","complete remission","partial remission","CR","PR","divergent","MR","CRr","NC","residual tumour","change","partial remission","no change","complete remission","minimal response","residual","tumour course","lymph node metastases","distant metastases","spread","residuals">
			copyright = <"© HiGHmed">
			use = <"To represent the status of a tumour disease during the course of treatment or after treatment and follow-up.
Use
This archetype shall be used to present assessments of the status of the tumour locally, overall, and in the areas of distant metastases and regional lymph nodes during the course of treatment or after treatment and follow-up.

The tumour status is important for assessing the success of the therapy and describes the changes in the tumour after the (primary) treatment. It shall be determined whether, for example, tumour tissue is still present; whether there is progression with existing residual tumour; no changes with existing residual tumour or a local recurrence.
In addition, this archetype presents the course status in the areas of distant metastases and regional lymph nodes.

This archetype can be embedded in the slot \"Specific Details\" of the parent archetype \"Problem/Diagnosis\" (openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis).">
			misuse = <"Must not be used to represent a disease status outside of the tumour disease.">
		>
	>
